+CONFIG_BT_HCIUART=y
+CONFIG_BT_HCIUART_H4=y
 # CONFIG_BT_UART_IN_AUDIO is not set
 # CONFIG_BT_HCIBCM203X is not set
 # CONFIG_BT_HCIBPA10X is not set
```

Enabling `CONFIG_BT_HCIUART` adds ~`hci_ldisc.o` + `hci_h4.o`; no other Kconfig dependency
changes are needed (`TTY=y` at :1567). Note that `CONFIG_BT_UART_IN_AUDIO` stays off, so
`bcm43xx.c` simply omits the `port->ops->set_wake()` calls (all such code is under that
ifdef); the GPIO-based BT_WAKE path remains active.

